course: dictionary
lesson: 4865
title: Iceman: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Iceman can be a name, a job from the past, or a nickname. The sentence around it tells you which one. «Ötzi the Iceman lived about 5,300 years ago» is about a real person, because the name Ötzi comes first and the years show it is a very old mummy.
explain: Look for clues. Words like «delivered», «ice» and «before fridges» show that an iceman was a man who brought blocks of ice to homes. A word about staying cool in a big moment, like «pressure», shows the word is a nickname for someone calm.
explain: Notice the capital letter. When The Iceman is a name, it has a capital letter, like Ötzi. When iceman is an ordinary noun, it has a small letter. Check the sentence: if it would still make sense with a different person's name, the word is a name.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check. Ask yourself: does a man frozen in the Alps for 5,300 years fit here? If yes, you have found the right meaning.
fact: An iceman is a noun. An icemen is the plural, for more than one man.
fact: The Iceman, called Ötzi, is a 5,300-year-old mummy found frozen in the Alps in 1991.
fact: Ötzi lived in the Copper Age. His copper axe, bow and arrows were kept safe in the ice.
fact: Before electric fridges, an iceman was a man who delivered blocks of ice to homes for iceboxes.
fact: A nickname «the Iceman» means someone who stays very calm under pressure.
exercise: «Ötzi the Iceman lived about 5,300 years ago.» What is the Iceman in this sentence? | A man frozen in the Alps for thousands of years | A man who sells ice cream from a van | * A mummy of a man found frozen in the Alps in 1991 | A calm player in a sports team
exercise: Before fridges, what did an iceman do? | Delivered letters to houses in winter | Kept the fridges in the shops cold | Made ice cream for the summer fair | * Brought blocks of ice to homes for iceboxes
exercise: Sam kept calm when the match was tied, so his coach called him «the Iceman». What does this nickname mean? | He was often late for training | He was cold and wore a coat | * He stays very calm under pressure | He was frozen in the ice for years
test: «Ötzi was found with his copper axe, bow and arrows.» Which two words are a name and need capital letters? | arrows | * The Iceman | ötzi | copper
test: Which meaning fits «the iceman came up the street with a block of ice»? | A calm person under pressure | A sports nickname | * An old job, a man who delivered ice | A famous mummy in the Alps
exam: Read «The Iceman tells us how people lived in the Copper Age.» Is the Iceman a name, a job or a nickname here? | A kind of fridge, because it keeps things cold | A nickname, because it means a calm person | * A name, because it is a capital letter and means Ötzi | A job, because it means a man who delivered ice
